181 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 325 0 R
/E (The Karlsruhe Dynamo Experiment: While Riga realized a single-scale, localized helical screw dynamo \(Ponomarenko model\) producing an oscillating, rotating magnetic field, the Karlsruhe facility demonstrated a homogeneous two-scale alpha square-dynamo. Using 52 spin-generator channels \(helically linked sodium ducts\), it showed how small-scale helical fluid motions organize to produce a large-scale, stationary magnetic dipole.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 326 0 R
/E (Solar Flux-Transport Dynamos & Magnetic Cycles: Explore how the combined action of differential rotation \(Omega-effect\) and meridional circulation creates the 11-year/22-year solar cycle and sunspot butterfly diagrams, connecting the periodic phase behavior of Riga's magnetic eigenmodes to stellar magnetic cycles)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 327 0 R
/E (Creating a feedback loop simulation: As we discussed, the Navier-Stokes momentum equation and the induction equation works together to obtain a saturation regime in the moving fluid. Now this dependancy can possibly be simulated to generate magnetic fields and that simulation can be probed to obtain a possibly cost-effective way to perform some propective experiments. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
